  "notes": [
    "Illustrative synthetic weights, not estimated market frequencies or claims about material quality.",
    "Effective weights are base times applicable emphasis and positioning multipliers, normalised over valid options.",
    "Hard concept eligibility is applied before weights. Named streams keep unrelated draws independent.",
    "Leather bias is an editable first positioning example, not a general quality rule; synthetic premium products remain possible.",
    "Packages express coherent construction combinations, not a new product hierarchy or guaranteed performance.",
    "Size, colour and width are canonical SKU identity here; sandal widths get separate retailer pages.",
    "Execution is independent of brand/positioning/emphasis and shared across a product's SKUs. Review fit and experience vary by person.",
    "Reference prices are authored SEK ranges. Review value uses the recorded purchase price; no current cheapest-retailer claim is implied.",
    "Manufactured widths are drawn as a joint set with regular (canonical standard) always present. Regular-only is most likely; wide and narrow availability are positively correlated.",
    "Draw one to four colours, then weighted distinct colours without replacement. Palette weights depend on concept, not positioning, emphasis or material."
  ],
